      "title": "Career Planning",
      "description": "Career Planning Services | King's College Skip to main content Search Kingâs College Search MENU Close Search Search Academics Academics Overview Majors & Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Special Programs Colleges & Centers Online Courses Academic Experience Academic Advisement Academic Success Career Planning Study Abroad D. Corgan Library Academic Planners Registrar's Office Admission Admission Overview Undergraduate Admission Admission Events First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Find Your Counselor Young Scholars Program Graduate Admission Admission Events Graduate Degrees Snapshot Graduate Cost & Aid Graduate Resources Contact Us Request Info Chat Apply Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Overview Cost Cost of Attendance Types of Aid King's Scholarships Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Forms Business Office Policies and Publications File your FAFSA Campus Life Campus Life Overview Get Involved Campus Activities Athletics The Arts Campus Ministry Shoval Center Campus Essentials Housing Dining Counseling Center Student Health Center Division of Student Affairs Student Handbook Orientation About About Overview General Information King's at a Glance Mission & History Accreditations and Rankings Campus Map Connect with Us Alumni & Friends Giving to King's Career Opportunities Social Media Red & Gold Gala Athletics News Events Give to King's MyKing's Search Visit Apply Home Academics Career Planning (Current Page) Career Planning The Office of Career Planning’s promotes lifelong career satisfaction by educating and empowering students to develop academic management, career, and professional skills; encourage faculty and staff support of student's career aspirations; and maintain a hospitable environment that enables employers to meet their recruiting needs. We offer a broad range of services from credit-bearing academic courses, individualized career counseling, and professional development activities, programs, and events. Resources Our staff is dedicated to meeting your individual needs, whether you’re a current student, alumnus, or recruiting employer! Our office is open Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. with individual appointments available upon request. Students and alumni Schedule an appointment with a career services professional here . Register on Handshake to post your resume and view recently posted job and internship openings Employers can find recruiting opportunities here . Find us by entering the Mulligan Physical Science Center from the interior campus side, then make an immediate left through the double wooden doors. The Office of Career Planning is located in Mulligan Physical Sciences Center, Room 95, the former location of the Office of Academic Advisement. Address 133 North River St. Mulligan Physical Sciences Center, Room 95 Wilkes-Barre, PA 18711 (570) 208-5874 Meet the Team Christopher C. Sutzko , Ed.D., M.S., LPC, CRC JCTC Director of Career Planning christophersutzko@kings.edu Alyssa Duffy, MHA ’17, ’18 Assistant Director of Career Planning alyssaduffy@kings.edu Theresa M. Kinney , M.S. Employer/Corporate Relations Coordinator theresakinney@kings.edu Academics Overview Academic Programs Academic Programs Online Courses Online Courses Academic Essentials Academic Essentials Registrar's Office Request a Transcript Verifications Core Curriculum CORE Structure CORE Goals and Outcomes CORE Courses and Contacts Academic Planners Undergraduate Flatsheets Minor Academic Planners Graduate Flatsheets Academic Success Academic Success Academic Advisement Placement Testing and Exemptions Advisement Process Changing Courses or Major Academic Standing and Alerts Academic Skills Center Accessibility, Accommodations, and Disability Services SPARK Program Academic Skills Resources The Tutoring Center The Writing Center KC Pathways First Generation Monarchs Hispanic and Latino Excellence Center Programs for Adult Learners Programs for Students Library D.